   "source_control": {
    "piece": "prism5_l15",
    "proof": "PENTAGON DOUBLE-LATTICE MARKED RETURN\n15 October 2026\n\nSource reading: Kallus and Kusner, arXiv:1509.02241, sections 2.2, 2.3, 3.1,\nhttps://arxiv.org/html/1509.02241 . The infinite construction is attributed\nto Greg Kuperberg and Wlodzimierz Kuperberg (1990); the explicit coordinates\nare reconstructed from Kallus and Kusner. No source optimality is claimed as\nnew, and no plane-optimality assertion is needed for the finite witnesses.\n\nUse native unit-edge pentagon vertices k0,...,k4 counterclockwise from the\npositive x axis. Let p1=k0, p4=(k2+k3)/2, p2=(k0+3k1)/4, p6=(3k4+k0)/4.\nThe two return generators are b0=p1-p4 and b1=2(p2-p6). The latter is the\ncomposition of two actual point reflections through p2,p6; the former is\ntwice a chord of the inscribed half-length parallelogram. A source word\n(i,j,t) realizes B(i,j)+m_t+R_t K, where m0=0,m1=2p2 and R0=I,R1=-I.\n\nThe exact canonical quartic field verifies every one of the 34 nontrivial\nordered motif/short-word comparisons, using support of R_a K-R_b K rather\nthan an assumed central symmetry. For every omitted word some |zi|>=2;\nthe corresponding center coordinate exceeds 2R because 2Bii-mi>2R and every\nbase vertex has coordinate absolute value at most R. This is a complete\nperiodic proof, not an empirical neighborhood check. Source_control retains\nall axes, supports, short words, tail slacks, and the four marked points.\n\nExtrude over the full height [-L/2,L/2] and add period (0,0,L). Equal vertical\nindices inherit the proved planar separator; different indices separate on\nz. The second frame is the proper spatial halfturn diag(-1,-1,1), with the\nexact native quaternion (0,0,0,1). Thus no owner is reflected improperly.\n\nFinite operation: cut complete owners around an actual source boundary mark,\nincluding p2,p6 with their native vertex indices and barycentric weights.\nFor each target count preserve the full source word, motif label, initial\ncenter and host scale. At every continuation step select a separator that\nalready separates the preceding whole-owner pair; restore all host walls\nsimultaneously in one common linear system. Keep the resulting full centers,\nall pair indices, every predecessor and fixed motif frame. A failed solver\nis retained as a complete predecessor, not treated as an obstruction.\n\nThe published source receives a common 1.000001 dilation before numerical\nrealization. Native witnesses scale final centers by 1.0000001 and use the\nsame host factor plus 1e-7. Every native whole-owner pair and host wall is\nthen checked by the official exact-input verifier. Finite gains are compared\nagainst both the full pinned public tree including community files and the\nstrongest retained own witness. Source density alone does not establish a\nfinite gain; all counts pay their actual boundary costs.\n",
